<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12298"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 26, 2005 - 9:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mail  from Curious <BR> <BR>I have a thought about Factor X. I am sure you folks have dissected that one a zillion times. I remember reading from crimelibrary the semen at the crime scene was unique to the extent that 6-7% of men had it. Now 6-7% isn&#39;t THAT unique. It was never clear what was so unique about it -- genetic deformity? illness? interesting cross-breeding marker? Then I read on the catchbtk.com site that his grandparents were first cousins and his parents were second cousins &#40;which though not verified hasn&#39;t been disputed on the site&#41;. That is pretty odd -- does the family practise inbreeding and if so, why? Did they have someone important in their ancestry and wanted to preserve that link? Was inbreeding their way of leaving a marker? Would it explain why a family member, according to kerri&#39;s website, is a genealogist?  <BR> <BR>I had a discussion with someone on why they tried to get Kerri&#39;s DNA and not Brian&#39;s. You guys know better -- maybe it&#39;s a state jurisdiction thing, that Michigan allowed it and whatever state Brian is in didn&#39;t allow it. It may be something or it may be nothing, as to why they chose Kerri and not Brian. My friend said they simply wanted to find out if Kerri was his real daughter, since most people hadn&#39;t thought BTK capable of consumation. Then I read on your site it could be possible one of the brothers donated sperm to help a sibling out. It just gets stranger and stranger. Whatever the reason, I&#39;d like to know why the LE chose Kerri and not Brian. Did they know something we didn&#39;t?  <BR> <BR>Now here&#39;s a random thought. When you started the thread on the three dudes,  I got really intrigued. Because I had not been 100% convinced he acted alone. He may have killed alone, that I can believe. But he may or may not have ACTED alone. My theory is if he&#39;s into S&amp;M, he would be the master and had a slave. He may have had the slave pick him up or do some other errands &#40;make that Nancy Fox call? do some drops? pick up trophies?&#41; and the slave may never have known what the master was up to -- he may have noticed the master was sexually aroused or agitated but never wondered why &#40;in the way slaves dare not practise free thought&#41;. BTK being so sick, I am not past thinking the slave could be a sibling or a relative. Especially if as above, the X factor had something to do with some kind of inbreeding that made they feel special, allowed to do certain things, maybe even encouraged to do certain things. <BR> <BR>I remember that DR was arrested a brother said they got the wrong guy but hey if Dennis did do it, God help him. I always thought that was a bit weird. You&#39;re either shocked and outraged or outraged and defending your brother but to have that kind of reaction is a bit strange. ``O no, he couldn&#39;t have... Dennis BTK? No..... hmmm, o wait. Right.... well..... ok, maybe..... if so..... ah......we leave it to God eh......&#39;&#39;    A pretty strange pattern of thought if you ask me. It told me two things: there was enough doubt about Dennis. There was also enough oddness about that reaction for me to suspect a family member. Normal people don&#39;t react like that. <BR> <BR>Thanks for even reading my mail. If it&#39;s way dumb, you dont have to post it. Just some loose ends I keep thinking about.  <BR> <BR>&#40;Personal note not for publication: mental illness appears to run in my family. So I have grown up watching them get depressed, suicidal, paranoid, obsessive compulsive. I used to fear it was genetic &#40;though quite certain it was from domestic abuse&#41; and my time would come and went to see doctors but they said in my siblings&#39; cases there was evidence of abuse that may have caused or aggravated it, ie nurture not nature. I don&#39;t know if they said it to make me feel better but hey,  I am always alert to any deficiency. I was spared the abuse as i was the last child and parents already too old to hit me I guess. My friends say I am so sane something must have gone right but they cant figure out why my family has such a high incidence. Police have been called to my house for domestic violence in my childhood and i myself witnessed a near homicide attempt. But I am saying all this to mean: I have seen close up enough strange family behavior and reactions to know something isn&#39;t quite right. I think DR&#39;s brother&#39;s reaction isn&#39;t quite right. He may know something. Like maybe another brother could have done something that implicated DR? I.e. I am suggesting he knows DR did it, and he had help but since he cannot protect DR now, he can protect that someone else&#41; <BR> <BR>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
