<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12477"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 8:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;...In daily life I&#39;d suspect BTK to be very unassuming, in the opinions of those around him. However, I think a close examination of his social sphere, even his family, would show a history of people &#39;getting bad vibes&#39;, or feeling that he could be inappropriate. Not in the sense of taking liberties...I&#39;ve said before, this doesn&#39;t seem like a guy who would ever get in trouble for something as alpha male as say groping a woman...he&#39;d be more likely to say off-color things. He&#39;d be the guy who takes a lewd, or sick joke too far. He will probably have a history of &#39;pushing it&#39; with those whom he is comfortable with. He is the kind of person who I think may make people around him uncomfortable in a way they can&#39;t ever pin down, and I bet a lot of them feel guilty for feeling that way. Because I also feel he may seem altruistic to those whom he&#39;s worked with and socialized with, say, at church...&#34; <BR> <BR>&#34;...I believe a couple of interesting things about his appearance; he does have a mustache, and has probably worn one for years, and he wears glasses. The frames will be larger than actually necessary for his face, and heavy. They will make him appear almost jowly, even if his weight is normal. He will be known, too, by some, like women whom he has worked with, as a starer. Always polite, perhaps, accomodating, but very watchful, intent...&#34; <BR> <BR>&#34;I think perfection, cleanliness, order, are all extremely important to him...&#34;  <BR> <BR>&#34;...I think in his own mind he has a definite moral code, and may still go to church regularly. If not, I bet he knows his bible cold. He is either an evangelical lutheran or perhaps even a southern baptist, though that will not be the denomination he was familiar with growing up...&#34; <BR> <BR>&#34;...I wonder if he worked a job for a good deal of his life that he regarded as far beneath him, his intellect. I would think it was a job that required cleanliness and order, and though he knew the job was beneath him he still took great pride in these two things. <BR> <BR>I bet he more closely resembles the mustached, &#39;dark&#39; drawing, but has probably always resented the inference he might be latino or perhaps Italian...&#34; <BR> <BR>&#34;...I thought of the Air Force tech school in Wichita Falls, TX.It&#39;s one of those danged gut things on my part, and the bias I referred to might be the fact my own Dad studied there in the early 70&#39;s. There is just some ineffable nagging thing there that keeps telling me air force...&#34;  <BR> <BR>&#34;...I had a malevolent daydream once where an older, balding gentleman with dark hair and a mustache, who was a bit jowly and wearing a tan members-only style jacket over a yellow and red plaid shirt, wore aviator-frame prescription glasses with a tint &#40;not sunglasses, but regular glasses that perhaps darkened in the sunlight&#41;, was standing on the driveway outside, staring at me through the bedroom window. This approximated a vision, I suppose, as I did not actually perceive him there - that would have been psychosis - but had the image of this man come so vividly and forcefully into my mind that the hair stood up on the back of my neck and I forced myself to get away from the computer and watch a South Park DVD...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>Tallulabay, I wrote all the above before February 25, 2005. This is proven - there are internet records, server date/time stamps I have no access to, that back it up. What I wrote above is only a portion of what I wrote. Several things I wrote along with what you read above were also decidedly wrong - I figured he&#39;d be single, he wasn&#39;t, I believed the stuff about railroading, and it was a lie - but if you read my words above you will see that I was accurate in some key places. <BR> <BR>- I surmised he&#39;d be lutheran <i>&#40;or baptist&#41;</i>. <BR> <BR>- I predicted he&#39;d be notably compulsively neat. <BR> <BR>- I predicted that he did look like the &#34;dark&#34; suspect description, and particularly that he&#39;d have kept his mustache. I predicted that he would be balding and wear a combover, and his style of prescription glasses. His driver&#39;s license photo, the only one where he&#39;s wearing a full beard, proved that.  <BR> <BR>- I was fairly sure that he was Air Force, that he attended the tech school at Sheppard in Wichita Falls, TX, and I said so.  <BR> <BR>- I had a &#34;vision&#34; that I still say was pure imagination of the man standing outside, on my property, in my driveway, wearing a tan jacket with epaulets - his Park City compliance officer shirts were tan with epaulets. <BR> <BR>- I said those at his church would think him altruistic - one of the stories seen a lot in the press is how the altruistic-seeming Rader and his wife even dropped off spaghetti and salad the Wednesday before his arrest at church supper, in spite of not being able to be there themselves. <BR> <BR>Yet, I do not claim to be psychic. I&#39;ve wondered a little, sure - especially after my very clear visualization that ended up being remarkably close - when I finally saw Rader&#39;s mugshot, I said to myself, &#34;THERE you are.&#34; <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s my point. I&#39;m not trying to James Randi you, really. But I&#39;ve presented evidence, over and over, complete with links to the original writings in other places, that I had thoughts, conclusions,  even &#34;visions&#34; that were inarguably close once we saw and learned about Dennis Rader. I reviewed my writing and wanted to call attention to things because I personally was amazed and wanted the insight others might have into what I did right. It&#39;s been suggested to me several times now by others that what I experienced was just flat-out psychic. Why are you claiming to be psychic, then, and where is that proof? I&#39;ve got proof, and yet I make no such claim. If I wanted I could easily claim psychic ability, but I&#39;m still not making that leap. The only proof I have, in my mind, is that I have good powers of deduction and an ability to draw, on occasion, pretty accurate conclusions.  <BR> <BR>I guess I&#39;m wondering what your point is. You say things that make little sense to me - <i>&#34;...for I say facts can be backed up in science as maps and geological profiling, whereas the latter cannot,but has been in 7 major murder cases as proved to the owners of this board...&#34;</i> - what do you mean, geological profiling? Are you speaking of psycho-geo<i>graphical</i> profiling as practiced by Dr. Maurice Godwin and a few others? If you don&#39;t feel the need to prove psychic ability, can you at least say which &#34;7 major murder cases&#34; you are talking about? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m asking you to help us make some clear sense of your words, because I for one am having trouble doing so.  <BR> <BR>You spoke of <i>&#34;...the great academics on this site...&#34;</i> and I couldn&#39;t tell where you were coming from with that - sarcasm or respect. Frankly, I must tell you, that&#39;s the very reason this is now the only BTK forum I bother with reading or posting to anymore. With thinkers like Ivy Leaguer, with the kaleidoscopic, almost beat-poet-like musings of a Lost Dog, with Victor&#39;s &#40;VSCantu&#41; snarky, smart humor, just to name a <i>few,</i> this messageboard sets itself above the others in general IQ points and discourse. Bring me those great academics over those who claim psychic ability - without a shred of actual proof presented, at all - every time. They are a pleasure and a relief after all the insane burblings found on other forums.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
