<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12543"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 4:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>After reading your excerpt of one of Tall&#39;s posts it occurred to me that she or he might be writing but the word/definitions do not fit the meaning the writer is attempting to convey.  .  .   <BR> <BR>&#34;Geological locations.  .  .  &#34; seems that Tall meant to say geographical. Geology is the study of the structure of the earth aka the earth&#39;s physical features NOT location.  .  .  what is &#34;pure&#34; psychology ? <BR> <BR>Frankly this person sounds like a bored high school kid who is running a con.  .  .  no legit scientist with &#34;gifted&#34; inteligence communicates giberish.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
